# FranVision Job Generator -- Dropbox sync configuration.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder) and fill in the real values.
# ".env" is gitignored -- never commit real credentials.
#
# Where these come from:
#   DROPBOX_APP_KEY / DROPBOX_APP_SECRET -- from your Dropbox App Console
#     (https://www.dropbox.com/developers/apps) for the app you created.
#     The app needs these scopes enabled: files.content.write,
#     files.metadata.write, file_properties.write, file_properties.read.
#   DROPBOX_REFRESH_TOKEN -- a long-lived refresh token for that app
#     (obtained once via Dropbox's OAuth2 flow with token_access_type=offline).
#     The SDK uses this to mint fresh short-lived access tokens automatically
#     on every call -- never hardcode a short-lived access token instead,
#     it will expire.
#   DROPBOX_TEMPLATE_ID -- printed by scripts/setup-dropbox-template.js the
#     one time you run it. Leave blank until you've run that script.

DROPBOX_APP_KEY=
DROPBOX_APP_SECRET=
DROPBOX_REFRESH_TOKEN=
DROPBOX_TEMPLATE_ID=

# --- Shared job server (optional; Supabase, see supabase/schema.sql) ---
# With all three set, the SERVER assigns Job IDs and stores job/draft
# metadata (so Mac + Windows never collide and share drafts). Unset = the
# old local-only behavior. JG_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is the project's public
# anon key; JG_TOKEN is this machine's own secret (its sha256 is registered
# in the jg_tokens table -- delete that row to revoke a lost machine).
JG_SUPABASE_URL=
JG_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
JG_TOKEN=

# --- Wave invoicing (optional; wave-backend.js, wraps ../wave-invoicing/) ---
# With WAVE_TOKEN + WAVE_BUSINESS_ID set, the Wave customer picker works and
# a Create/Update Job can build a Wave draft invoice. Unset = both are
# skipped entirely, same as before this existed.
#   WAVE_TOKEN -- a Wave full-access API token (Wave account settings ->
#     API/manage apps). Never commit the real value.
#   WAVE_BUSINESS_ID -- the Wave business id to invoice against (base64-ish
#     opaque string, e.g. from a `business(id:...)` GraphQL query -- see
#     wave-probe/ in the core-schema branch for how this was found).
#   WAVE_AUTO_INVOICE -- '1' to actually create/update a DRAFT invoice on
#     Create/Update Job (only when a Wave customer was picked in the form).
#     Unset/'0' = the picker still works but no invoice is ever created --
#     the safe default while this is new.
#   WAVE_PRODUCT_MAP_PATH -- optional override; defaults to
#     job-generator/wave-product-map.json (gitignored -- see
#     wave-product-map.example.json for the shape). Maps pricing-config.js
#     service/package ids (+ 'adjustment_discount'/'custom_item') to real
#     Wave product ids in that business -- required before any invoice can
#     actually be built (the picker/search work without it).
WAVE_TOKEN=
WAVE_BUSINESS_ID=
WAVE_AUTO_INVOICE=
WAVE_PRODUCT_MAP_PATH=
